From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RJ Skerry-Ryan <rryan@alum.mit.edu>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:45:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmgr-misc: Treat a missing pstate register as
 absent

devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname() returns an error pointer, not
NULL, when the named register is missing. The probe stored that pointer
as the register base and the suspend and resume callbacks then
dereferenced it.

Check for an error pointer so that a PMGR without one of the fabric or
DCS pstate registers only drives the one it has.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: RJ Skerry-Ryan <rryan@alum.mit.edu>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-pmgr-misc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-pmgr-misc.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-pmgr-misc.c
index 53170aad4d..9b6a5c89f8 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-pmgr-misc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-pmgr-misc.c
@@ -448,7 +448,7 @@ static bool apple_pmgr_init_device(struct apple_pmgr_misc *misc,
 
 	base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(
 		to_platform_device(misc->dev), name);
-	if (!base)
+	if (IS_ERR(base))
 		return false;
 
 	val = readl_relaxed(base + APPLE_CLKGEN_PSTATE);
